              "text": "**Mundra Port** is the **largest private commercial and container port in India**. \n\n### Key Details:\n* **Location:** It is located on the northern shores of the **Gulf of Kutch** near Mundra in the Kutch district of **Gujarat, India**. \n* **Ownership and Operation:** It is owned and operated by **Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone Limited (APSEZ)**, a part of the multinational conglomerate Adani Group. Originally established as India's first private port, it has grown exponentially since it began operations in the late 1990s.\n* **Type of Port:** It is a **deep-draft, all-weather port**, meaning it can operate year-round and is capable of handling some of the world's largest giant cargo vessels (including fully-laden Very Large Crude Carriers\u2014VLCCs).\n\n### Why is it significant?\n* **High Cargo Volume:** It is a major maritime gateway, handling over 150 million metric tonnes (MMT) of cargo annually (even surpassing the 200 MMT milestone in a single year). \n* **National Trade Hub:** Mundra Port handles roughly **11% of India's total maritime trade** and more than **33% of its container traffic**. \n* **Diverse Capabilities:** The port has 26 berths and specialized terminals capable of handling multiple types of cargo, including containers, dry bulk (such as coal), liquid cargo, crude oil, breakbulk, and automobiles. \n* **Special Economic Zone (SEZ):** It is integrated with the Mundra Special Economic Zone, making it a massive industrial and logistics hub. \n* **Strategic Connectivity:** The port has dedicated, privately-owned rail lines and strong road links that seamlessly connect it to landlocked industrial centers in North and Northwest India.",
